// Title: Dllhost.EXE Execution Anomaly
// Sigma ID: e7888eb1-13b0-4616-bd99-4bc0c2b054b9
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-06-27 | Modified: 2023-05-15
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, stealth, T1055
// Description: Detects a "dllhost" process spawning with no commandline arguments which is very rare to happen
//   and could indicate process injection activity or malware mimicking similar system processes.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://redcanary.com/blog/child-processes/
//   - https://nasbench.medium.com/what-is-the-dllhost-exe-process-actually-running-ef9fe4c19c08
//   - https://www.ncsc.gov.uk/static-assets/documents/malware-analysis-reports/goofy-guineapig/NCSC-MAR-Goofy-Guineapig.pdf
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_dllhost_no_cli_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\dllhost.exe" and (ProcessCommandLine in~ ("dllhost.exe", "dllhost"))) and (not(isnull(ProcessCommandLine)))
